# The example and test fixtures are byte-exact: no BOM, LF only, and no trailing
# newline. Git's autocrlf would rewrite them on checkout under Windows and hand
# the next user exactly the corruption this skill exists to prevent.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf

# -text marks these as binary so git never normalizes their line endings.
# tests/bad-crlf-bom.txt is INTENTIONALLY CRLF-with-BOM: it is the fixture that
# proves check 1 of the validator fires. Do not "fix" it.
*.txt -text
